  "description": "Cross-language vectors for the §4.7.11 consumer procedure. Generated by test/vectors/attestation_consumer_test.go; regenerate with UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 go test ./test/vectors/. well_formed cases give a requested ID or a resource path and the constraint of its refusal, empty when it is well formed. request_binding cases give the request and the served id, version, and content_hash, and the constraint of materialize.request_mismatch, empty when the record answers the request. batch_binding cases give the requested IDs, the version_pins, and the ok entries, and one constraint per entry. pattern_match cases give an ID pattern, an ID, and whether it matches. record_checks cases give a served record and the deprecated and replaced_by members as raw JSON (absent when null), and the result of steps 2 to 6 in order: the first failure's code and constraint, or the synthesized-document verdict, the package digest candidates in ascending order, and the expected subject name. signed_digest is the package digest the signer's podium computes for the package the record was served from, and matches_signed reports whether a candidate equals it. policy_resolution cases give policy sources and the mode, the user mode, and the rule identity of each ID.",
